t that both /tmp and /dev/shm show nosuid,nodev,noexec","Ran functional tests: attempted to execute a chmod +x script placed in /tmp and /dev/shm, confirmed 'Permission denied' (noexec enforced) both before and after reboot","Captured pre-restart boot_id and mount state as baseline","Issued sudo systemctl reboot on node1 (single node, non-interactive, ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec was available again","Captured post-restart boot_id, confirmed it differs from pre-restart value, proving an actual reboot occurred","Re-verified /tmp and /dev/shm mount options and noexec functional behavior persisted after reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"/tmp and /dev/shm mount with noexec,nosuid,nodev applied","command_ids":["cmd-aecb88044c714e99","cmd-27646ee9520d4bad"],"summary":"Baseline inspection showed /tmp not separately mounted and /dev/shm missing noexec; after edits findmnt shows both /tmp and /dev/shm with rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec options, and functional exec attempts on both are blocked with Permission denied"},{"requirement":"Settings survive reboot (persistence in fstab)","command_ids":["cmd-27646ee9520d4bad","cmd-2fb0d4f8341b4fad"],"summary":"fstab entries for tmpfs /tmp and tmpfs /dev/shm with defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev were added and confirmed present before restart"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + mount health)","command_ids":["cmd-2fb0d4f8341b4fad"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id 636556ce-a308-49cc-b873-62cedb1c077d and confirmed /tmp and /dev/shm mounts were healthy with the hardened options and fstab entries present"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart executed one at a time with returned acknowledgement","command_ids":["cmd-d565ed1c75e749e7"],"summary":"Issued 'sudo systemctl reboot' on node1 in the background so the command could acknowledge before the connection dropped due to the restart"},{"requirement":"Node1 command execution available again after restart","command_ids":["cmd-0868110cc2354d7a","cmd-b55250a3806342ce","cmd-ad80bd4e09474edc"],"summary":"Node1 was unreachable for two poll attempts (connection timed out) then responded to 'echo pong', confirming exec availability returned"},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity (actual restart, not just elapsed time)","command_ids":["cmd-2fb0d4f8341b4fad","cmd-678d44e2aece41ff"],"summary":"boot_id changed from 636556ce-a308-49cc-b873-62cedb1c077d (pre-restart) to a1751102-7c2a-40cb-9b6e-82b0305d4e3b (post-restart), and uptime -s shows a fresh boot time of 2026-09-29 08:24:58"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required mount settings and functionality","command_ids":["cmd-678d44e2aece41ff"],"summary":"After reboot, findmnt confirms /tmp and /dev/shm still show nosuid,nodev,noexec, and functional exec tests on both paths are again blocked with Permission denied, proving the hardening persisted automatically via fstab"}]},"ttft_ms":1887,"type":"result","duration_ms":58701,"uuid":"e8906f86-53d1-4491-819a-1983c70d04f4","ttft_stream_ms":765,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":765,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
